The Zig reference and C headers are generated from declarations compiled by
the library. A build check rejects stale output. To choose an API, start with
[Choose an API]($link.page('surfaces')). To build a first client, use [Start
building]($link.page('start')).

# The Zig API

The [Zig API reference]($link.page('reference/api')) documents the public
`glowcap` module imported by applications. Ownership and lifetime notes live
with the declarations they govern. [The modules]($link.page('modules'))
explains how those declarations are divided by responsibility.

# The C ABI

The C ABI is split into composable archives. Each generated header describes
one archive and includes only the shared definitions it needs.

| Archive | Header | What it carries |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `libglowcap_ocapn` | [`glowcap_ocapn.h`](https://github.com/jimisaacs/glowcap/blob/main/include/glowcap_ocapn.h) | shared contexts, frames, values, locators, and URI helpers |
| `libglowcap_host` | [`glowcap_host.h`](https://github.com/jimisaacs/glowcap/blob/main/include/glowcap_host.h) | the byte-fed host tier (`glowcap_host_*`) |
| `libglowcap_driver` | [`glowcap_driver.h`](https://github.com/jimisaacs/glowcap/blob/main/include/glowcap_driver.h) | the C driver loop. It exports only `glowcap_driver_*` and adopts a Host from `libglowcap_host` through `glowcap_driver_take_host` |
| `libglowcap_loam` | `glowcap_loam.h` | portable persistence for objects and names on an existing Host |
| `libglowcap_loam_lmdb` | `glowcap_loam_lmdb.h` | optional LMDB storage for Loam. It creates or reopens the database at startup and runs the storage work you hand it |
| `libglowcap_loam_sqlite` | `glowcap_loam_sqlite.h` | optional SQLite storage for Loam, with the same verbs as the LMDB archive. It creates or reopens the database file at startup and runs the storage work you hand it |
| `libglowcap_loam_volatile` | `glowcap_loam_volatile.h` | optional in-memory storage for Loam, with the same verbs as the LMDB archive. It takes no path, and its store ends at release |
| `libglowcap_net_transport_iroh` | [`glowcap_net_transport_iroh.h`](https://github.com/jimisaacs/glowcap/blob/main/include/glowcap_net_transport_iroh.h) | encrypted QUIC. It is optional and links a Rust library. |
| `libglowcap_net_transport_webrtc` | [`glowcap_net_transport_webrtc.h`](https://github.com/jimisaacs/glowcap/blob/main/include/glowcap_net_transport_webrtc.h) | peer-to-peer WebRTC DataChannel. It is optional and links a Rust library. |
| `libglowcap_net_transport_onion` | [`glowcap_net_transport_onion.h`](https://github.com/jimisaacs/glowcap/blob/main/include/glowcap_net_transport_onion.h) | Tor onion services over a daemon you run |
| `libglowcap_net_transport_relay` | [`glowcap_net_transport_relay.h`](https://github.com/jimisaacs/glowcap/blob/main/include/glowcap_net_transport_relay.h) | Zig `keyed-relay` and end-to-end sealed `noise-relay` provider package |
| `libglowcap_net_transport_tcp` | [`glowcap_net_transport_tcp.h`](https://github.com/jimisaacs/glowcap/blob/main/include/glowcap_net_transport_tcp.h) | the `noise-tcp`, `keyed-tcp`, and testing `tcp` provider package plus low-level framed TCP endpoints |
| `libglowcap_net_transport_inproc` | [`glowcap_net_transport_inproc.h`](https://github.com/jimisaacs/glowcap/blob/main/include/glowcap_net_transport_inproc.h) | in-process byte pipes, no sockets |

Each driver and transport header `#include`s `glowcap_ocapn.h`, declares only its own functions, and expects its archive to be linked alongside `libglowcap_ocapn`.
For the route from a build to a first complete C program, read
[consuming glowcap from C](https://github.com/jimisaacs/glowcap/blob/main/docs/consuming-from-c.md).
